**Developed seventh common foundation:** orientation and angular motion, angular-momentum origins and transport, mass inertia and kinetic energy, axial work/impulse, rolling constraints and contact admissibility, internal exchange and observational ambiguity. Nine new lessons and two preserved mechanical lessons connect these concepts to an original exact investigation with 3,266 checks and a bounded published washer reconstruction. The existing OpenStax and Tong source identities retain actual inspection and reuse boundaries. Continue chemistry molecular identity and structure at comparable breadth; full mechanics and the physics core remain unfinished.


**Developed eighth common foundation:** microscopic states and preparation, constrained subsystems, statistical entropy, finite reservoirs and canonical weighting, fluctuations/correlations, controlled energy ladders, and relaxation versus equilibrium. Ten new lessons reuse counting, probability, thermodynamic and infinite-sum preparation plus the existing Tong source identity. An original exact investigation compares equal means with different constraints and equal equilibrium weights with different dynamics; 2,578 finite checks pass. Physics now has 98 common learning Records. Continue chemistry at comparable breadth; statistical mechanics, quantum theory, relativity, astronomy and the whole core remain unfinished.


**Developed common quantum foundations:** preparation and evidence, amplitudes and Born probabilities, finite spin observables, conditional instruments, mixtures/dephasing, state-dependent uncertainty, Hamiltonian dynamics, a bounded continuous-well bridge, composite states and calibrated count comparisons. Twelve original lessons reuse the complex-operator, wave, chemical-state and inquiry/statistical formation and three unchanged programs. Ideal source models are reconstructed without claiming laboratory reproduction. Physics now has 110 common learning Records. This prepares quantum-related branch entry; field integration, magnetic/inductive, relativistic/gravitational and astronomical foundations remain common gaps, and whole physics/quantum subjects remain unfinished. Continue computing human use/trust and engineering human operation before deeper specializations.


**Developed common magnetic and inductive foundations:** magnetic observation and force, signed uniform-field motion, steady-current geometry, oriented induction, moving boundaries, inductive storage, Maxwell consistency, field energy and propagation. Eleven original lessons connect three preserved electromagnetic lessons with bounded common-reading notes. An exact investigation checks deflection, boundary circulation, mechanical/circuit/field energy and a current-only parameter ambiguity; one published RL example is reconstructed. Physics now has 124 common learning Records. Spacetime/gravity and astronomical evidence remain common gaps before the same readiness review. Whole physics and its advanced branches remain unfinished.


**Developed common spacetime and gravity foundations:** events and clock comparison, Lorentz transformations, proper time, causality and received signals, relativistic energy, Newtonian gravity and orbits, local equivalence, tidal structure and weak gravitational clock effects. Twelve original lessons connect one preserved electromagnetic lesson and three bounded source Records. An exact investigation checks frame and orbital invariants, rival descriptions and a published optical-clock calculation. Physics now has 137 common learning Records. Astronomical evidence remains next before the same 134-scope readiness review. Whole physics and its advanced branches remain unfinished.


**Developed common astronomical foundations:** directions and epochs, parallax inference, detector counts, flux/magnitude/extinction, spectral meaning, planetary and binary evidence, stellar balances and populations, galactic mass and cosmic distances. Thirteen original lessons reuse the shared spacetime, quantum, thermal, chemical and inquiry preparation. An exact investigation checks observation models and ambiguities and reconstructs one historical distance/magnitude calculation. Physics now has 150 common learning Records. Review the same 134-scope mapping across all six areas before developing major branches; full astrophysics, astronomy and cosmology remain unfinished.


**Scope:** Explain and measure motion, energy, a circuit, or a wave; develop more rigorous accounts of a chosen system. Offer qualitative and quantitative entrances; add algebra, calculus, linear algebra, or statistical methods at the steps that actually use them.

